      "text": "Just in case you're wondering why I'm so bullish on legacy memory...\n\nTheir hikes seem a lot extreme than $NBIS reported +17-21% GPU rentals today or Taiyo-Murata type MLCC hikes. \n\nPrice hikes projections expected for H2:\n\n- SLC NAND: +120-170% in H2 vs H1\n- High-capacity NOR: +90-110% in H2 vs H1\n- ~DDR3/DDR4: +50% Q3\n- DDR2: +35-40% in Q3\n- LPDDR: +20% or more in Q3\n- DDR1, older LPDDR and PSRAM: also rising\n\nAs a consolidated view... \n\nLot of these are stacked off existing hikes H1, (eg. 130-150% for H1 SLC NAND), so you get +406%-575% cumulative throughout 2026.\n\nWhich impacts blended net",
